### RepFrame REST API Tests
### Use with VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
### Base URL: http://localhost:5055

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5055
@exerciseId = {{exerciseId}}
@setId = {{setId}}
@workoutSessionId = {{workoutSessionId}}

### ============================================================
### EXERCISES
### ============================================================

### Get all exercises (empty initially)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/exercises
Accept: application/json

### Create a new exercise - Bench Press
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/exercises
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bench Press",
  "muscleGroup": "Chest"
}

### Create a new exercise - Squat
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/exercises
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Squat",
  "muscleGroup": "Legs"
}

### Create a new exercise - Deadlift (no muscle group)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/exercises
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Deadlift",
  "muscleGroup": null
}

### Get all exercises
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/exercises
Accept: application/json

### Get exercise by ID (replace with actual ID from create response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/exercises/{{exerciseId}}
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================
### WORKOUT SESSIONS
### ============================================================

### Create a new workout session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workout-sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Get all workout sessions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workout-sessions
Accept: application/json

### Get active workout session (returns 404 if none)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workout-sessions/active
Accept: application/json

### Get workout session by ID (replace with actual ID from create response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workout-sessions/{{workoutSessionId}}
Accept: application/json

### Finish active workout session (replace with actual ID)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workout-sessions/{{workoutSessionId}}/finish
Content-Type: application/json


### ============================================================
### SETS
### ============================================================

### Create a new set - Bench Press 3x10 @ 80kg
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workoutSessionId": "{{workoutSessionId}}",
  "exerciseId": "{{exerciseId}}",
  "number": 1,
  "weightKg": 80.5,
  "reps": 10,
  "rir": 2,
  "type": "standard"
}

### Create a new set - Squat 4x8 @ 100kg (RIR not specified)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workoutSessionId": "{{workoutSessionId}}",
  "exerciseId": "{{exerciseId}}",
  "number": 2,
  "weightKg": 100.0,
  "reps": 8,
  "rir": null,
  "type": "standard"
}

### Create a new set - incline dumbbell press (failure)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workoutSessionId": "{{workoutSessionId}}",
  "exerciseId": "{{exerciseId}}",
  "number": 3,
  "weightKg": 35.0,
  "reps": 12,
  "rir": 0,
  "type": "failure"
}

### Get all sets
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sets
Accept: application/json

### Get set by ID (replace with actual ID from create response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sets/{{setId}}
Accept: application/json

### Delete a set (replace with actual ID)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/sets/{{setId}}
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================
### ERROR CASES
### ============================================================

### Get non-existent exercise (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/exercises/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json

### Create set with invalid exercise ID (should return 400 or 500)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workoutSessionId": "{{workoutSessionId}}",
  "exerciseId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "number": 1,
  "weightKg": 50.0,
  "reps": 10,
  "rir": null,
  "type": "standard"
}

### Delete non-existent set (should return 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/sets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json
